# What must never enter a build context.
#
# `web.Dockerfile` does `COPY . .` for the build stage, so without this file `.env` would
# be baked into an image layer. Multi-stage does not save you: the runtime image is clean,
# but the intermediate layer still holds the secret and anyone who can pull the build
# cache can read it. `.gitignore` has no bearing on Docker at all — the two lists are
# unrelated, and assuming otherwise is the usual way credentials reach a registry.
#
# Everything below is also a build-speed measure: the context is uploaded to the daemon
# before the first instruction runs, and node_modules alone is hundreds of megabytes.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*-key.json
gha-creds-*.json
service-account*.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- vcs and tooling
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- dependencies
node_modules
**/node_modules
.venv
**/.venv
.pnpm-store
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- build output
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist
coverage
**/coverage

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- not needed at build
docs
scripts/hooks
**/*.md
!README.md
# Full-resolution source art, deliberately unserved — ~900KB that would otherwise ride
# along in every image.
apps/web/assets
